@startuml initiator_withdrawal_protocol_development
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
title Initiator Withdrawal Protocol Development View

box "Initiator peer" #AliceBlue
actor User_0 as User #LightCyan
participant Iso_0 as Iso #LightBlue
participant Boomlet_0 as Boomlet #LightPink
participant ST_0 as ST #Violet
participant Niso_0 as Niso #LightGreen
end box
participant WT #Red
participant Other_Peers as Peers #White
participant SARs #Yellow
participant Bitcoin #LightGray

autonumber "<b>[WI00]"

note over User, SARs
  <b>Scope</b>
  Peer 0 denotes the initiator role for this ceremony, not a fixed setup index.
  Peer-indexed collections contain exactly one entry per setup peer in setup order.
  Guards and detailed-message coverage are in withdrawal_development_contracts.md.
end note

note over Boomlet #LightYellow
  <b>Boomlet withdrawal states</b>
  IDLE -> REVIEWING_TX -> APPROVED -> COMMITTED -> DIGGING
  -> READY_TO_SIGN -> SIGNING -> SIGNATURE_EXPORTED -> IDLE
end note

group Initiator review and approval
User -> Niso: WI-REVIEW-1  candidate PSBT
note over Niso #Pink: Accept under G-WITHDRAWAL-PRECONDITIONS and G-PSBT-PREVALIDATION
Niso -> Boomlet: WI-REVIEW-2  PSBT and current local block height
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Independently accept under G-WITHDRAWAL-PRECONDITIONS and G-PSBT-AUTHORIZATION.
  Derive tx_id, create fresh ST review nonce, IDLE -> REVIEWING_TX.
end note
Boomlet -> ST: WI-REVIEW-3  Enc_ST(TxReview{tx_id, nonce}) via Niso
ST -> User: WI-REVIEW-4  trusted display of tx_id
User -> ST: WI-REVIEW-5  approve exact intended tx_id
ST -> Boomlet: WI-REVIEW-6  Enc_Boomlet(Sig_ST(exact TxReview)) via Niso
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Accept under G-TX-REVIEW-APPROVAL.
  Derive withdrawal_id from setup_instance_id, tx_id, initiator identity, and fresh approval nonce.
  REVIEWING_TX -> APPROVED
end note
Boomlet -> WT: WI-APPROVE-1  withdrawal_id, Enc_WT(Sig_Boomlet(TxApproval_0)), Enc_Boomlet_i(PSBT) x4 via Niso
note over WT #Pink: Accept under G-INITIATOR-APPROVAL-AT-WT; create Sig_WT(WtTxApproval)
WT -> Peers: WI-APPROVE-2  WtTxApproval, initiator TxApproval, recipient-encrypted PSBT
Peers -> WT: WI-APPROVE-3  Enc_WT(Sig_Boomlet_i(TxApproval_i)) x4
note over WT #Pink: Accept under G-TX-APPROVAL-COLLECTION; canonicalize in setup peer order
WT -> Boomlet: WI-APPROVE-4  ordered five TxApprovals and WtTxApproval via Niso
note over Niso #Pink: Prevalidate under G-APPROVAL-SET-AT-PEER
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Revalidate under G-APPROVAL-SET-AT-PEER.
  approved_withdrawal_id := H(withdrawal_id, exact ordered five-approval set).
end note
end

group Attestation gate and commitment
par Initiator prepares its commitment
  ref over User, ST, Boomlet
    W-DURESS-CHECK
    Fresh nonce-bound challenge; valid response yields safe or duress placeholder plaintext.
  end ref
  note over Boomlet #Lavender: Create Sig_Boomlet(TxCommit_0) and fresh approved_withdrawal_id-bound Placeholder_0
  Boomlet -> WT: WI-COMMIT-1  Enc_WT(Sig_Boomlet(TxCommit_0 + Placeholder_0)) via Niso
  note over Boomlet #Lavender: APPROVED -> COMMITTED
  note over WT #Lavender: Authenticate, verify, and stage initiator commit
else Non-initiators prove approval-set receipt
  Peers -> WT: WI-COMMIT-2  Sig_Boomlet_i(ApprovalSetAttestation) x4
end
note over WT #Pink
  G-APPROVAL-ATTESTATIONS opens only with one valid matching attestation from every non-initiator.
  The open gate permits initiator placeholder relay, initiator commit acknowledgment,
  and acceptance of non-initiator commits.
end note
WT -> SARs: WI-COMMIT-3  Placeholder_0, Boomlet identity, approved_withdrawal_id
note over SARs #Pink: Accept and durably process under G-SAR-PLACEHOLDER; release at the fixed observable deadline
SARs --> WT: WI-COMMIT-4  Enc_Boomlet_0(Sig_SAR_0(exact Placeholder_0))
note over WT #Pink: Accept initiator commit under G-TX-COMMIT-AT-WT
WT -> Peers: WI-COMMIT-5  Sig_WT(Sig_Boomlet_0(TxCommit_0))
Peers -> WT: WI-COMMIT-6  Enc_WT(Sig_Boomlet_i(TxCommit_i + Placeholder_i)) x4
WT -> SARs: WI-COMMIT-7  each non-initiator Placeholder_i to its setup-bound SAR
SARs --> WT: WI-COMMIT-8  exact encrypted acknowledgment_i x4
note over WT #Pink: Accept every commit and SAR acknowledgment under G-TX-COMMIT-AT-WT
WT -> Boomlet: WI-COMMIT-9  complete WT-signed TxCommit set and acknowledgment_0 via Niso
note over Niso #Pink: Prevalidate under G-COMMIT-COLLECTION
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Revalidate complete set and exact own acknowledgment under G-COMMIT-COLLECTION.
  COMMITTED -> DIGGING.
  Draw one fresh private mystery only on DIGGING entry.
  Initialize counter := 0, ping_seq_num := 0, reached := false, last_seen_block := local block height.
end note
end

group Digging rounds
loop Until WT holds one current reached ping from every peer
  Boomlet -> WT: WI-DIG-1  Enc_WT(Sig_Boomlet(Ping_0 + freshly encrypted Placeholder_0)) via Niso
  Peers -> WT: WI-DIG-2  corresponding Ping_i and fresh Placeholder_i x4
  note over WT #Pink
    Handle exact retries under SPEC 15.7; return after receipt-only delivery.
    Accept each new ping under G-PING-AT-WT.
  end note
  WT -> SARs: WI-DIG-3  each ping's exact Placeholder_i
  note over SARs #Pink: Durably process each under G-SAR-PLACEHOLDER
  SARs --> WT: WI-DIG-4  exact encrypted acknowledgment_i x5
  note over WT #Pink
    A ping contributes to a pong only after its exact acknowledgment.
    Enforce round spacing; construct recipient-specific Pong_i from current signed pings of all other peers.
  end note
  WT -> Boomlet: WI-DIG-5  Enc_Boomlet(Sig_WT(Pong_0)), acknowledgment_0 via Niso
  WT -> Peers: WI-DIG-6  recipient-specific Pong_i and acknowledgment_i
  note over Niso #Pink: Prevalidate visible pong and collection properties under G-PONG-AT-BOOMLET
  note over Boomlet #Pink
    Revalidate under G-PONG-AT-BOOMLET.
  end note
  note over Boomlet #Lavender: Boomlet performs any requested consent rotation.
  opt After rotation or when selected by the profile cadence
    ref over User, ST, Boomlet
      W-DURESS-CHECK
      Consume one fresh phase-bound response and update placeholder plaintext.
    end ref
  end
  note over Boomlet #Lavender
    Evaluate G-COUNTER-ADVANCE before block-height catch-up.
    Increment only if the local chain advanced and every other current ping is within the local freshness window.
    Apply bounded last_seen_block catch-up after every valid pong, including no-progress rounds.
    Record reached flags monotonically; set local reached when counter >= mystery; increment ping_seq_num.
    Freshly encrypt the current placeholder plaintext for the next ping.
    A reached Boomlet continues participating until all five current reached pings are collected.
  end note
end
end

group Reached collection and signing
WT -> Niso: WI-FINAL-1  Sig_WT(reached_pings_collection)
WT -> Peers: WI-FINAL-2  same signed reached_pings_collection
note over Niso #Pink
  Accept under G-REACHED-COLLECTION.
  Hydrate the PSBT without changing transaction semantics, ordering, sighash policy, or tx_id.
end note
Niso -> Boomlet: WI-FINAL-3  reached_pings_collection and hydrated PSBT
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Revalidate under G-REACHED-COLLECTION and G-HYDRATED-PSBT.
  DIGGING -> READY_TO_SIGN
end note
Niso --> User: WI-SIGN-1  connect Boomlet to Iso
User -> Iso: WI-SIGN-2  mnemonic, passphrase, network, account, key index
Iso -> Boomlet: WI-SIGN-3  begin MuSig2 session
note over Boomlet #Lavender: READY_TO_SIGN -> SIGNING; create session-bound Boomlet nonce
Boomlet -> Iso: WI-SIGN-4  verified signing package and Boomlet public nonce
note over Iso #Pink: Accept package under G-MUSIG2-SIGNING
Iso -> Boomlet: WI-SIGN-5  normal public nonce and normal partial signature
note over Boomlet #Pink: Verify normal partial; create Boomlet partial; erase nonce material
Boomlet --> Iso: WI-SIGN-6  Boomlet partial signature
note over Iso #Pink: Verify Boomlet partial, finalize peer fragment, erase nonce material
Iso --> User: WI-SIGN-7  connect Boomlet to Niso
User -> Niso: WI-SIGN-8  request signed-fragment export
Niso -> Boomlet: WI-SIGN-9  export signed fragment
Boomlet --> Niso: WI-SIGN-10  psbt_signed_by_peer_0
note over Boomlet #Lavender
  SIGNING -> SIGNATURE_EXPORTED.
  Boomlet sends a final ping and waits for its exact SAR receipt and any required backup reset acknowledgment.
  under_duress := false
  Clear active withdrawal state and mystery; SIGNATURE_EXPORTED -> IDLE.
end note
Niso -> WT: WI-RELAY-1  psbt_signed_by_peer_0
Peers -> WT: WI-RELAY-2  psbt_signed_by_peer_i x4
note over WT #Pink: Accept under G-FINAL-FRAGMENTS; aggregate and verify the exact committed tx_id
WT -> Bitcoin: WI-RELAY-3  exact signed transaction
end

note over User, Bitcoin #LightYellow
  Invalid identity, signature, envelope, nonce, ceremony binding, sequence, block-height relation,
  collection, transaction, or state transition stalls the active ceremony.
end note

@enduml
